# Build context is the repository root (railway.json points at
# backend/Dockerfile, which leaves the context here). Keep the context to what
# the image actually needs: the backend tree, minus its build output and the
# large non-build subtrees vendored inside SGEE and sensen.

.git
*.log

frontend
node_modules
**/node_modules

backend/build
.next
out

docs
.playwright-mcp
.claude
config

backend/external/SGEE/web-lsp
backend/external/SGEE/vscode-extension
backend/BigBrotherAnalytics
backend/sensen/external/CosyVoice
backend/sensen/eval_samples
backend/sensen/demo_qwen3

# Kept in step with .railwayignore. backend/CMakeLists.txt:139-146 FORCEs
# BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS, BUILD_TESTS, BUILD_EXAMPLES and BUILD_BENCHMARKS off,
# and sensen guards add_subdirectory on exactly those options, so none of these
# is read during configure. Verified by parking all four and re-configuring.
backend/sensen/benchmarks
backend/sensen/tests
backend/sensen/python
backend/sensen/examples
backend/sensen/docs
**/*.nsys-rep
**/*.sqlite
**/perf.data*
**/core.*

# Both assistants' fine-tuned Qwen3-0.6B GGUFs (Q8_0, ~639 MB each) are fetched
# during the build from MODEL_URL / MORTGAGE_MODEL_URL and verified against
# MODEL_SHA256 / MORTGAGE_MODEL_SHA256 in backend/Dockerfile's `model` stage.
# They must never arrive through the build context instead: `COPY backend/
# /src/backend/` in the builder stage has no verification step of its own and
# would carry whatever it found, unchecked, into the image -- which is exactly
# the substituted-or-truncated-GGUF failure the `model` stage exists to make
# impossible.
#
# backend/.dockerignore says the same thing and CANNOT enforce it here.
# railway.json sets `dockerfilePath: backend/Dockerfile` and leaves the context
# at the repository root, so the ignore file that applies is
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore (backend/Dockerfile.dockerignore, which does not
# exist) falling back to <context>/.dockerignore -- this file. backend/
# .dockerignore is only consulted by a build whose context is backend/, which
# this build is not. This entry is what actually keeps a .gguf out of the
# context, and it matters now rather than in the abstract:
# backend/models/mortgagefv-assistant-q8_0.gguf is 639 MB and is sitting in the
# tree today. .railwayignore excludes it from the `railway up` payload for the
# same reason (with its own note on the ~30 s upload deadline).
**/*.gguf

# EXCEPTION, added deliberately: the staged assistant models SHIP IN THE BUILD
# CONTEXT. They are the owner's proprietary weights and are deliberately not
# hosted on any external model registry, so the context is how they reach the
# image. The blanket rule above still catches a .gguf dropped anywhere else in
# the tree, which is the case it was written for.
#
# NARROWED TO THE ENCODERS ON 2026-10-03, and the scope of that is worth stating
# precisely because the obvious reading is wrong. `!backend/models/*.gguf`
# un-ignored EVERYTHING in that directory, and four 639 MB mortgage DECODERS had
# accumulated there (v2, v18, v19, v20) = 2.4 GB.
#
# THIS AFFECTS A LOCAL `docker build` AND NOT A RAILWAY DEPLOY. A first reading of
# this said every deploy shipped those 2.4 GB; it did not. `.railwayignore` carries
# its own `**/*.gguf` (line 115), so the uploaded tar contains NO .gguf at all --
# measured, the only member under backend/models/ is .gitkeep, on both of
# railway_deploy.sh's tar arms. The exception below has therefore been INERT for
# every Railway build, and the staged branches in backend/Dockerfile have never
# fired there: on Railway both encoders arrive from *_ENCODER_URL.
#
# It is still worth narrowing, for the build whose context IS this working tree.
# Nothing in the image uses those four files -- the decoder it would use arrives
# from MORTGAGE_MODEL_URL, and with both assistants on ENCODERS no decoder is
# loaded at all, because each worker constructor returns BEFORE touching one when
# its backend is `encoder`.
#
# The files are NOT deleted: they are the only copies of those GGUFs on this host
# (model-archive/ holds the bf16 safetensors, not the quantised files), so they
# stay on disk and stop being copied into a local build context. Widen this back
# to `*.gguf` the day a DECODER is staged deliberately, and say which one.
!backend/models/*-encoder*.gguf

# model-archive/ holds MERGED BF16 CHECKPOINTS -- the safetensors a training run
# produces, ~1.2-1.8 GB each, which are the INPUT to a GGUF conversion and reach
# the image through nothing. The `**/*.gguf` rule above does NOT cover them,
# because they are not .gguf, and that cost a failed deploy on 2026-10-01:
# `gzip: stdout: Disk quota exceeded` staging the upload tarball, with 5 GB of
# checkpoints in it. The tell is that the failure is in TAR, before Railway is
# reached at all, so it reads as a quota problem rather than as a missing
# exclusion.
#
# .gitignore got this entry the same day. TWO ignore files is two things to
# forget, and a weight file is exactly the shape that makes forgetting one
# expensive -- gitignored keeps it out of git and says nothing about the build
# context.
model-archive/

